Z||000000||RobertVol||04-30-2000||07:12 PM||||The one thing my Ttop 88 does not have is the factory sub. I can get one but I was wondering and this may be an ignorant question but I know nothing about radios and installing them.....Can you have the factory sub system without the factory radio ? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||04-30-2000||08:46 PM||||Not trying to put a damper on things but did you know the T-top cars require a special light fixture to house the slider? The normal Fieros are square and the T-top Fieros have the 2 rear corners modified to fit the T-tops. This is so the corners don't go into the opening.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobertVol||04-30-2000||09:32 PM||||Yeah I am aware. But thanks for speaking on that.This sub and bracket is from a 88 t top. I also have another solid roof GT that has a non factory radio in it and would like to a sub in that one also..||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-30-2000||10:54 PM||||You can hook-up the factory sub to an aftermarket radio, But it takes some creative wiring. I used to have a link to a website that had diagrams on how to do it but the link isn't working anymore. I think the basic thing was to hook the pink wire from the sub amp to the remote turn on of the radio and to use the factory wiring for the speakers. Sort of the adatpter harness that goes between the new radio and the stock harness connectors.||||reg||1
